---An action that Amazon SES can take when it receives an email on behalf of one or more email addresses or domains that you own. An instance of this data type can represent only one action.
---@class aws.ses.ReceiptAction
---@field S3Action? aws.ses.S3Action Saves the received message to an Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) bucket and, optionally, publishes a notification to Amazon SNS.
---@field BounceAction? aws.ses.BounceAction Rejects the received email by returning a bounce response to the sender and, optionally, publishes a notification to Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).
---@field WorkmailAction? aws.ses.WorkmailAction Calls Amazon WorkMail and, optionally, publishes a notification to Amazon Amazon SNS.
---@field LambdaAction? aws.ses.LambdaAction Calls an Amazon Web Services Lambda function, and optionally, publishes a notification to Amazon SNS.
---@field StopAction? aws.ses.StopAction Terminates the evaluation of the receipt rule set and optionally publishes a notification to Amazon SNS.
---@field AddHeaderAction? aws.ses.AddHeaderAction Adds a header to the received email.
---@field SNSAction? aws.ses.SNSAction Publishes the email content within a notification to Amazon SNS.
---@field ConnectAction? aws.ses.ConnectAction Parses the received message and starts an email contact in Amazon Connect on your behalf.

---@alias aws.ses.ReceiptActionsList aws.ses.ReceiptAction[]

