---Recipient-related information to include in the Delivery Status Notification (DSN) when an email that Amazon SES receives on your behalf bounces.
---@class aws.ses.RecipientDsnFields
---@field FinalRecipient? aws.ses.Address The email address that the message was ultimately delivered to. This corresponds to the Final-Recipient in the DSN. If not specified, FinalRecipient is set to the Recipient specified in the BouncedRecipientInfo structure. Either FinalRecipient or the recipient in BouncedRecipientInfo must be a recipient of the original bounced message.
---@field Action aws.ses.DsnAction|string The action performed by the reporting mail transfer agent (MTA) as a result of its attempt to deliver the message to the recipient address. This is required by RFC 3464.
---@field RemoteMta? aws.ses.RemoteMta The MTA to which the remote MTA attempted to deliver the message, formatted as specified in RFC 3464 (mta-name-type; mta-name). This parameter typically applies only to propagating synchronous bounces.
---@field Status aws.ses.DsnStatus The status code that indicates what went wrong. This is required by RFC 3464.
---@field DiagnosticCode? aws.ses.DiagnosticCode An extended explanation of what went wrong; this is usually an SMTP response. See RFC 3463 for the correct formatting of this parameter.
---@field LastAttemptDate? aws.ses.LastAttemptDate The time the final delivery attempt was made, in RFC 822 date-time format.
---@field ExtensionFields? aws.ses.ExtensionFieldList Additional X-headers to include in the DSN.

